---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import {FAQSection, RelatedArticles} from '../../components/article';

const title = 'Best Coworking Spaces in Lisbon 2025: A Digital Nomad\'s Guide';
const description = 'Discover Lisbon\'s top coworking spaces for digital nomads. Compare prices, amenities, locations, and vibes to find your perfect workspace in Portugal\'s capital.';
const author = 'FloatJet Team';
const authorUrl = '/about';
const pubDate = new Date('2024-12-22');
const readingTime = 13;
const image = '/images/unsplash/photo-1497366216548-37526070297c-1200w.webp';
const imageAlt = 'Modern coworking space with people working on laptops';

const headings = [
  {depth: 2, slug: 'introduction', text: 'Lisbon\'s Coworking Scene'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'top-coworking-spaces', text: 'Top 10 Coworking Spaces'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'comparison', text: 'Quick Comparison'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'day-pass-vs-monthly', text: 'Day Pass vs Monthly Membership'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'neighborhoods', text: 'Best Neighborhoods for Remote Workers'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'cafe-alternatives', text: 'Cafe Alternatives with Good WiFi'},
  {depth: 2, slug: 'faq', text: 'Frequently Asked Questions'}
];

const faqData = [
  {
    question: 'How much do coworking spaces cost in Lisbon?',
    answer: 'Day passes range from €15-30. Monthly hot desk memberships cost €100-200, while dedicated desks run €200-350. Private offices start around €400-600/month for small teams. Prices vary by neighborhood and amenities.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need to book in advance?',
    answer: 'For day passes, most spaces accept walk-ins but booking is recommended during busy periods. Monthly memberships usually require a tour and signup process. Some popular spaces have waitlists for dedicated desks.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What\'s the WiFi speed like in Lisbon coworking spaces?',
    answer: 'Most professional coworking spaces offer 100-500 Mbps symmetric fiber internet with backup connections. Always test the speed during a trial day before committing to a monthly plan.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I take video calls at coworking spaces?',
    answer: 'Yes, most spaces have phone booths or meeting rooms for calls. Hot desks in open areas are generally quiet-call friendly but not ideal for long video meetings. Some spaces have dedicated \"call zones.\"'
  },
  {
    question: 'Are coworking spaces good for meeting other nomads?',
    answer: 'Absolutely. Many Lisbon coworking spaces host events, workshops, and social activities. Some like Second Home and Heden are known for their strong communities. It\'s one of the best ways to build a network in Lisbon.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What if I only need a workspace occasionally?',
    answer: 'Day passes are perfect for occasional use. Some spaces offer punch cards (10 days for discounted rate) or part-time memberships (10-15 days/month). Cafe working is free but less reliable for long sessions.'
  }
];

const relatedArticles = [
  {
    title: 'Portugal Digital Nomad Visa Guide',
    excerpt: 'Everything you need to work legally from Lisbon.',
    href: '/guides/digital-nomad-visa-portugal',
    image: '/images/unsplash/photo-1555881400-74d7acaacd8b-800w.webp',
    imageAlt: 'Lisbon Portugal cityscape'
  },
  {
    title: 'Find Reliable WiFi Anywhere',
    excerpt: 'Tips for finding fast internet while traveling.',
    href: '/blog/find-reliable-wifi-anywhere',
    image: '/images/unsplash/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8-800w.webp',
    imageAlt: 'WiFi connectivity concept'
  },
  {
    title: 'Top Destinations for Digital Nomads',
    excerpt: 'Compare Lisbon with other nomad hotspots.',
    href: '/blog/top-destinations-digital-nomads',
    image: '/images/unsplash/photo-1488646953014-85cb44e25828-800w.webp',
    imageAlt: 'World travel destinations'
  }
];
---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Travel"
    categorySlug="guides/travel"
    headings={headings}
>
  <p class="lead">
    Lisbon has become one of Europe's top digital nomad destinations, and its coworking scene
    has exploded to match. From converted warehouses to sleek design spaces, here's your guide
    to finding the perfect workspace in Portugal's sunny capital.
  </p>

  <h2 id="introduction">Lisbon's Coworking Scene</h2>

  <p>
    Lisbon offers dozens of coworking spaces across the city, each with its own character. Whether
    you want a quiet professional environment, a social community hub, or something with a view,
    there's a space for you.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most spaces cluster in a few key neighborhoods: Chiado/Baixa (central), Santos (trendy),
    Principe Real (upscale), and Alcântara (waterfront). Prices and vibes vary significantly—
    a tour or day pass is worth it before committing monthly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="top-coworking-spaces">Top 10 Coworking Spaces</h2>

  <h3>1. Heden</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Community and networking</p>
  <p>
    Heden stands out for its tight-knit community of freelancers and remote workers. Regular
    events, a rooftop terrace, and a welcoming vibe make it easy to make friends. The space
    attracts creative professionals and startup founders.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Santos</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€175/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€20</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Rooftop, events, strong community</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. Second Home Lisboa</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Design and aesthetics</p>
  <p>
    Part of the global Second Home network, this space is stunning. Plants everywhere, colorful
    furniture, and natural light create an Instagram-worthy workspace. Higher prices reflect
    the premium experience.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Mercado da Ribeira (Time Out Market area)</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€250-350/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€30</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Beautiful design, great location, global network access</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Cowork Lisboa</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Budget-conscious nomads</p>
  <p>
    No-frills, affordable coworking in a central location. Clean, functional spaces with
    everything you need and nothing you don't. Great value for money if you prioritize
    location and basics over bells and whistles.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Baixa/Chiado</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€100-150/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€15</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Central location, affordable, straightforward</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. Avila Spaces</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> River views and modern amenities</p>
  <p>
    Located in the Avila tower, this space offers stunning Tagus River views and modern,
    professional facilities. Multiple floors provide options from open hot desks to private
    suites. Popular with established businesses and serious freelancers.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Parque das Nações</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€150-200/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€20-25</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> River views, modern building, parking available</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>5. Idea Hub</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Startups and entrepreneurs</p>
  <p>
    Positioned as a startup incubator as much as coworking space, Idea Hub attracts founders
    and early-stage companies. Good for networking with the Portuguese tech ecosystem and
    potential investors.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Saldanha</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€130-180/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€18</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Startup focus, mentorship, investment connections</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>6. Village Underground Lisboa</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Creative vibe</p>
  <p>
    Built from shipping containers and old buses, Village Underground is Lisbon's most unique
    coworking space. The creative, artistic atmosphere attracts designers, artists, and anyone
    who wants inspiration from their environment.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Alcântara</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€175/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€22</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Unique architecture, creative community, outdoor space</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>7. LACS</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Central location and flexibility</p>
  <p>
    Multiple locations across Lisbon make LACS convenient wherever you're staying. Professional
    environments with good facilities and flexible membership options. A safe, reliable choice.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Multiple (Conde d'Óbidos, Anjos, others)</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€140-200/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€18-25</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Multiple locations, professional, flexible plans</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>8. Sitio</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Events and social activities</p>
  <p>
    Sitio combines coworking with an active events calendar. If you want to attend workshops,
    talks, and social gatherings while you work, this space delivers community alongside
    workspace.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Príncipe Real</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€150-190/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€20</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Regular events, good neighborhood, terrace</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>9. Selina Secret Garden</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Coliving + coworking combo</p>
  <p>
    Part of the Selina network, this space offers both accommodation and coworking. Perfect
    if you're looking for an all-in-one solution when you first arrive. The garden area
    provides a pleasant outdoor work option.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Intendente</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€150/month (coworking only)</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€20</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Coliving option, garden, hostel vibe</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>10. Impact Hub Lisbon</h3>
  <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Social impact and sustainability focus</p>
  <p>
    Part of the global Impact Hub network, this space attracts social entrepreneurs and
    sustainability-focused businesses. Strong programming around impact topics and access
    to the global Impact Hub community.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Location:</strong> Beato</li>
    <li><strong>Hot desk:</strong> ~€160-200/month</li>
    <li><strong>Day pass:</strong> ~€20</li>
    <li><strong>Highlights:</strong> Mission-driven community, global network, event space</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="comparison">Quick Comparison</h2>

  <h3>By Price (Monthly Hot Desk)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Budget (€100-150):</strong> Cowork Lisboa</li>
    <li><strong>Mid-range (€150-200):</strong> Heden, LACS, Avila Spaces, Idea Hub, Sitio, Impact Hub</li>
    <li><strong>Premium (€200+):</strong> Second Home, Village Underground</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>By Vibe</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Social/Community:</strong> Heden, Sitio, Selina</li>
    <li><strong>Professional/Quiet:</strong> Avila Spaces, LACS</li>
    <li><strong>Creative:</strong> Village Underground, Second Home</li>
    <li><strong>Startup-focused:</strong> Idea Hub, Impact Hub</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>By Location</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Central:</strong> Cowork Lisboa, Second Home, LACS</li>
    <li><strong>Waterfront:</strong> Avila Spaces, Village Underground</li>
    <li><strong>Trendy neighborhoods:</strong> Heden (Santos), Sitio (Príncipe Real)</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="day-pass-vs-monthly">Day Pass vs Monthly Membership</h2>

  <h3>When Day Passes Make Sense</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>You're in Lisbon for less than 2 weeks</li>
    <li>You want to test multiple spaces before committing</li>
    <li>You only need coworking 1-2 days per week</li>
    <li>You're combining cafe work with occasional coworking</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When Monthly Memberships Make Sense</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>You're staying for a month or longer</li>
    <li>You need workspace most days</li>
    <li>You want community and networking opportunities</li>
    <li>Day passes would cost more than monthly over your stay</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Money Math</h3>
  <p>
    If day passes cost €20 and monthly hot desk costs €150, the break-even is 7-8 days. If
    you'll use coworking more than 8 days per month, monthly membership saves money.
  </p>

  <h2 id="neighborhoods">Best Neighborhoods for Remote Workers</h2>

  <h3>Chiado/Baixa</h3>
  <p>
    Central, touristy, but convenient. Good for short stays when you want to be near everything.
    Higher accommodation costs but walkable to many coworking spaces, restaurants, and transport.
  </p>

  <h3>Santos/Cais do Sodré</h3>
  <p>
    Trendy riverside area with good nightlife. Popular with nomads and young professionals.
    Home to Heden and close to Second Home. Good balance of local and international vibes.
  </p>

  <h3>Príncipe Real</h3>
  <p>
    Upscale, quiet, and green. Beautiful gardens, nice cafes, slightly higher prices. Good
    for those wanting a more residential feel while staying central.
  </p>

  <h3>Alfama/Mouraria</h3>
  <p>
    Historic, hilly, and charming. Fewer coworking spaces but authentic Lisbon character.
    Good for those who prefer cafe work and don't mind walking up hills.
  </p>

  <h3>Alcântara/Belém</h3>
  <p>
    Waterfront area with converted industrial spaces. Home to Village Underground and LX
    Factory (cultural hub). Slightly removed from center but excellent for creative types.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cafe-alternatives">Cafe Alternatives with Good WiFi</h2>

  <p>
    Not every day requires a coworking space. Here are reliable cafes for occasional laptop work:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Copenhagen Coffee Lab:</strong> Multiple locations, great coffee, work-friendly</li>
    <li><strong>Fábrica Coffee Roasters:</strong> Specialty coffee, outlets available, quiet mornings</li>
    <li><strong>Hello, Kristof:</strong> Nomad favorite, good WiFi, relaxed about laptop workers</li>
    <li><strong>Ler Devagar (LX Factory):</strong> Bookstore cafe, unique atmosphere, good for shorter sessions</li>
    <li><strong>Wish:</strong> Healthy food, spacious, work-friendly atmosphere</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <strong>Cafe etiquette:</strong> Buy something every 1-2 hours, avoid peak lunch times, and
    be mindful of taking up tables for hours during busy periods.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <FAQSection faqs={faqData}/>

  <h2>Find Your Perfect Lisbon Workspace</h2>

  <p>
    Lisbon's coworking scene has something for everyone. Start with day passes at 2-3 spaces
    that match your priorities—community, location, price, or vibe. Once you find your fit,
    commit to a monthly membership and settle into the routine.
  </p>

  <p>
    The best coworking space is the one you'll actually use and enjoy. In Lisbon, you're
    spoiled for choice.
  </p>

  <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
</ArticleLayout>
